  "prefLabel": "Rep 500 ETHICAL STANDARDS, PROFESSIONAL CONDUCT, ADMINISTRATIVE FINES AND LICENSE SURRENDER--REPEALED",
  "recordType": "rule-chapter",
  "ruleText": "Rep 500\n\n#9153, effective 5-2-08\n\n#10967, effective 10-31-15\n\nThe Executive Director subsequently readopted with amendments Chapter Plc 1200 as a regular rule in Document #13704, effective 8-1-23. thereby replacing the former interim rule for Plc 1200 in Document #13547. Amendments in Document #13704 included adding new definitions of “criminal records check” in Plc 1202.04, “military spouse” in Plc 1202.10, and “on active military duty” in Plc 1202.11. Document #13704 also extensively amended Part Plc 1204 on initial licensure and Part Plc 1206 on renewal of licenses, including insertion of new rules and deletion of existing rules, to apply the procedures on initial licenses, temporary licenses, and renewal of licenses in Chapter Plc 300. These amendments necessitated the renumbering of other existing rules in Part Plc 1204 and Part Plc 1206 that had been filed in Document #13547.",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1200.html"
